course: dictionary
lesson: 6970
title: Pandemic: a disease across the world
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A pandemic is an outbreak of an infectious disease that spreads across many countries or the whole world and makes very many people ill. The disease passes from person to person, so it can travel very quickly.
explain: Use the context clues. «In 2020 it spread across the whole world because nobody's body knew it yet» tells you the disease reached everywhere. «A pandemic is a new disease spreading across many countries because nobody has immunity yet» tells you why it spread: immunity means the body's protection against a disease, and nobody had it.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The pandemic spread across the world» still makes sense with "a worldwide outbreak of disease" in place of pandemic, so your meaning is right. Remember: an epidemic is a big outbreak in one area, but a pandemic is worldwide.
fact: A pandemic is an outbreak of disease that spreads across many countries or the whole world.
fact: «Pandemic» can also be an adjective, meaning spreading everywhere, as in «a pandemic illness».
fact: An «epidemic» is a big outbreak in one area; a pandemic is worldwide.
fact: The COVID-19 pandemic is a recent example: schools closed, people wore masks, and vaccines were made.
fact: The Black Death and the great flu after the First World War were pandemics in history.
exercise: «A pandemic is a new disease spreading across many countries.» What is a pandemic? | A hospital department for urgent problems | A type of money | A shop that sells medicine | *An outbreak of disease that spreads across many countries or the whole world
exercise: What is the difference between an epidemic and a pandemic? | *An epidemic is a big outbreak in one area; a pandemic spreads worldwide | An epidemic is worldwide; a pandemic is in one small town | A pandemic is always a cold, and an epidemic is always a flu | They mean exactly the same thing
exercise: «It was reported that NHS waiting lists grew very long, especially after the COVID pandemic.» Find and copy the one word that names a worldwide outbreak of disease. | waiting | NHS | long | *pandemic
test: «In 2020 it spread across the whole world because nobody's body knew it yet.» What does this sentence tell you about the disease? | It only affected animals | It was easy to cure | It stayed in one village | *It spread everywhere in the world
test: In history lessons, which of these is an example of a pandemic? | *The Black Death | A school trip to a museum | A birthday party with many guests | A new bus route in town
exam: Jayden says, «A pandemic is just a bad cold.» Which answer is best? | Yes, a pandemic is only ever in one house | No, a pandemic is a kind of medicine | Yes, every cold is a pandemic | *No, a pandemic is an outbreak spreading across many countries or the whole world, not just one cold
